Installing nantic_widgets
=========================

Prerequisites
-------------

 * Python 2.7 or later (http://www.python.org/)
 * trytond (http://www.tryton.org/)

Installation
------------

Once you've downloaded and unpacked the nantic_widgets source
release, enter the directory where the archive was unpacked, and run:

    python setup.py install

Note that you may need administrator/root privileges for this step, as
this command will by default attempt to install module to the Python
site-packages directory on your system.

For advanced options, please refer to the easy_install and/or the distutils
documentation:

  http://peak.telecommunity.com/DevCenter/EasyInstall
  http://docs.python.org/inst/inst.html

To use without installation, extract the archive into ``trytond/modules`` with
the directory name widgets.

Vector fields (PostgreSQL)
--------------------------

Install the Python adapter with ``pip install 'nantic_widgets[vector]'``
and enable the pgvector extension in each database that uses Vector fields::

    CREATE EXTENSION IF NOT EXISTS vector;

Configure Tryton to load the database mixin at server startup::

    [database]
    database_mixins:
        trytond.modules.widgets.database.DatabaseMixin

If other database mixins are configured, keep them in the same list,
one per line. Restart the server after changing the configuration.

The mixin registers the pgvector adapters on each connection, independently
of statement_timeout. It logs a warning when the vector type is unavailable.
The register_vector patch to Tryton's PostgreSQL backend is no longer needed.
